cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite the associated article."
title: "Conditional modal branch selection in physics-informed active control of lid-driven cavity flow: identification, reproducibility, and independent numerical verification"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and figures for the conditional selection of modal branches in
  physics-informed active control of a lid-driven cavity (Re = 500, aspect ratio 1),
  where the actuation-energy budget E* = 0.25 is held identical across the four
  compared control classes (uniform, stationary second harmonic, mixed
  spatio-temporal, pure temporal). The study identifies which modal branch is
  physically admissible, documents the reproducibility of the selection, and
  verifies it independently with a lattice Boltzmann MRT solver. Includes the
  vendored LBM-MRT solver, the PINN module of the companion work, the 15 PINN
  seed checkpoints used to build the controls, and the full reproduction
  pipeline with SHA256 verification.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/geminiahmed25-Ahkat/conditional-modal-branch-selection-lid-driven-cavity"
